&f(3) = 6, \\
&f(5) = 4, \\
&f(7) = 2, \\
&f(9) = 0.
\end{aligned}
\]
We can see that \( f \) is a cyclic function with a period of 8, as \( f(f(f(f(f(f(f(f(x)))))))) = x \). This means that applying \( f \) repeatedly will eventually cycle back to the original value.

To determine the number Larry writes on his tenth finger after starting with 3 on his pinky finger, we need to compute the value of \( f(f(f(f(f(f(f(f(f(3)))))))) \).

