Since the probability of it not snowing on each of the next three days is the same and the events are independent, the probability that it will not snow at all for the next three days is the product of the probabilities that it will not snow on each of those days. Thus, the probability that it will not snow at all for the next three days is \(\left(\frac{1}{4}\right)^3 = \frac{1}{64}\).

So, the final answer is \(\boxed{\frac{1}{64}}

